    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">Inverse proportion refers to a relationship where one quantity increases as the other decreases, such that the product of the two quantities is constant. Graphically, this creates a curve called a reciprocal curve, which approaches but never touches the axes. The constant <em>k</em> is the product of the two variables, so if <em>y = k/x</em>, then <em>xy = k</em>.</p>",
